    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1506">

                <pb facs="1216" n="1100" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1100"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/428.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 18.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 7, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith
                    triplicate copies of the Official Gazette, dated March 29, 1912, containing
                    Spanish text of the law enacted on March 20, 1912,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1506-f1"/> by the Nicaraguan National Assembly, authorizing an
                    additional supplementary [loan?] of Brown Brothers and Company, and J. and W.
                    Seligman and Company, of New York, as reported in my telegram of the latter
                    mentioned date. No translation thereof has been made, as I am informed that the
                    Department has already been furnished with the official English text prepared by
                    the bankers.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">George T. Weitzel.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
